From 1ef5c5cee2eeb389ee5367b885990b1c66ea4b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:53:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/91] deepseek4 : sparse attention in prefill - D11 on
 P13-style chunks, each query its own FlashAttention stream over its picks and
 window (SiegeLadder D10 step 1, LLAMA_DSV4_SPARSE_PREFILL=1, off by default)

A compressed layer's prefill attention ran over the ring rows of its chunk and every compressed position up to its widest
query, the indexer's top-k only a 0 / -inf mask - the quadratic part of a long prompt. A ubatch whose queries all see at
least top-k compressed positions in both groups, at consecutive positions with their whole window in the ring, now
attends sparsely: chunks of LLAMA_DSV4_SPARSE_QC (512) queries, each query a FlashAttention stream of its own over 768
rows gathered per query (512 picks, 128 window rows by position, 128 dummies of its own row under -inf) from the
compressed K and the ring joined once per layer, straight to F16 (ggml_get_rows_f16, new; CUDA already wrote F16 rows,
CPU path added). One mask row shared by all streams - flash_attn_mask_to_KV_max read a mask shared across streams
(ne33 < ne03) out of bounds (sequence*s33): fixed to (sequence % ne33)*s33 as the main kernel reads it. Other ubatches
(the first ~1024 positions) keep P13 or the attention of before; the pp graph is reserved twice (sparse and not). Not
bitwise (another summation order). Agent draft, reviewed. SiegeLadder runs.md 4.119: test-backend-ops GET_ROWS 124/124,
FLASH_ATTN_EXT 2924/2924; the default decode path untouched (n1p text = trace, counters = o32); P13 unchanged (its 4.106
KL to the digit); kl_run 4K context, -ub 2048: KLD 0.00075 vs P13 chunks (floor of a prefill change 0.00078); the 30K
document at -ub 6144: 95.9 s with P13 -> 80.7 s (368 tok/s), the answer's 128 tokens: same text, KL 0.0027.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
